-- title:
--   Lemma 5.3, p. 15 — the measure π of Lemma 5.1 is stationary for the MBI
-- statement:
--   Let $(X,\mathbb P)$ be an MBI with parameters $(\alpha,\mu,p,\beta,\nu,q)$ and let $\pi=(\pi(k))_{k\ge0}$ be the nonnegative measure of Lemma 5.1. Then $\pi$ is a **stationary measure**: for all $y\ge0$ and $t\ge0$,
--   $$\sum_{x\ge0}\pi(x)P_t(x,y)=\pi(y).$$
--
--   When $\beta>0$ or $q>0$ the measure $\pi$ is positive, so it can serve as the reference measure of Section 3 for the MBI.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: parameter constraints of p. 12 (α > 0, µ, ν probability measures, µ(0) > 0, µ(1) = 0, p, β, q ≥ 0) → MBIParams.Valid, with HasSum µ 1, HasSum ν 1 and ν(0) = 0; reason: same constraints
--   - encoding: E = ℤ ∩ [0, ∞), states x, y ≥ 0 → Set.Ici (0 : ℤ), with natural-number arguments cast to ℤ; reason: same states
--   - encoding: the Markov chain (X, ℙ) generated by Q (jump chain/holding time definition, p. 2) → transition, resolvent, hitProb, hitBeforeProb, exitDist, killedResolvent computed from jump-chain path sums with Exp(1) holding clocks; reason: this is the paper's construction (i)–(iv); the cemetery ∂ is represented by leaving E
--   - encoding: π on E → π extended by 0 to negative integers; the identity in ℝ≥0∞ via ofReal; reason: π ≥ 0, so ofReal is injective on its values
-- source:
--   Loeffen, Patie, Wang, Fluctuation Theory of Continuous-Time, Skip-Free Downward Markov Chains with Applications to Branching Processes with Immigration, arXiv:2208.14425v1, p. 15, Lemma 5.3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Chain
import Definitions.Def_SkipFreeFluct_MBI_Model
open scoped ENNReal Topology
open Filter MeasureTheory

namespace SkipFreeFluct.MBI

/-- Lemma 5.3, p. 15. The nonnegative measure `π` of Lemma 5.1 (extended by `0` to negative
integers) is a stationary measure for the MBI: `∑_{x ≥ 0} π(x) P_t(x, y) = π(y)` for all
`y ≥ 0`, `t ≥ 0`. -/
theorem lemma_5_3 (P : MBIParams) (hP : P.Valid) :
    IsStationaryMeasure (Set.Ici 0) (mbiQ P)
      (fun x : ℤ => if 0 ≤ x then piSeq P x.toNat else 0) := by sorry

end SkipFreeFluct.MBI
